---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RuntimeDecisionSequence from "../components/diagrams/RuntimeDecisionSequence.astro";
import ArchitecturePlanes from "../components/diagrams/ArchitecturePlanes.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Product | BeaconGuard Authorization and Assurance"
  description="BeaconGuard independently authorizes exact consequential AI actions under customer-approved policy authority, fails closed on DENY, and preserves verifiable decision evidence."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <p class="section-label">PRODUCT</p>
    <h1>Independent authorization for consequential AI actions</h1>
    <p class="lead">BeaconGuard sits between a proposed AI action and the enterprise side effect it would create.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>The authorization model</h2>
    <RuntimeDecisionSequence />
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Three responsibilities</h2>
    <div class="section-grid section-grid--compact">
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Govern</h3><p>Customer-approved controls become verified production policy authority.</p></div>
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Authorize</h3><p>BeaconGuard evaluates the exact material action before execution.</p></div>
      <div class="content-card"><h3>Verify</h3><p>Decision evidence preserves the action, governing authority, and outcome for later verification.</p></div>
    </div>
    <ArchitecturePlanes />
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Where identity, MCP, and A2A fit</h2>
    <p>
      Identity answers who is acting. Delegation answers for whom. MCP, A2A, and application controls can establish invocation scope. Permission to use a tool does not mean permission to perform every action it can trigger. BeaconGuard authorizes the specific consequential action before execution.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Request ALLOW does not equal Action ALLOW.</strong></p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/trust-assurance">Review Assurance</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">How It Works</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/docs/architecture">Technical Reference</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
